From 8ccca2606f77d36cbbba366e2ee7c26b1195f115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:53:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: output-sink quote pairing,
 echo/printf producers, pin `| grep bash` (review 5890784121)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three gaps review 5890784121 found in #2127's output-sink walk (all also
allowed on base, not #2127 regressions):

1. Quote pairing. `_iter_printed_shell_payloads` paired '…' and "…" from text
   start, so a stray apostrophe in the other kind (`print("it's")`, a
   `# don't` comment) shifted single-quote pairing and a later
   `print('bash /x/huge.sh')` under `| bash` was never yielded. The literal
   regexes are now lookaheads: the span after EVERY quote up to the next of
   its kind is yielded. The between-quote spans dedupe, so the line cap is
   unchanged (print-generator under `| bash` first refuses at ~8.2k lines,
   plain body ~16.5k, same as base; measured).
2. Non-heredoc producers. `printf 'bash /x/huge.sh\n' | bash` kept the `\n`
   glued to the path, and `echo bash /x/huge.sh | bash` has no quoted
   literal. Every yielded literal is now also yielded with `\n\t\r\v\f`
   escapes turned into newlines, and under a sink the argument line of every
   executed `echo`/`printf` (wrappers, `{ … }`, `then`/`do` peeled) is
   yielded too. The extra tokenization pass runs only when the text mentions
   echo/printf.
3. `| grep bash` / `| grep -c bash` count as sinks (any later pipe word is
   the shell): fails closed, intended. Documented in output_reaches_shell
   and pinned as positive cases; `| grep bashrc` pinned negative next to
   `| grep bash.sh`.

Corpus: SINK_CONSUMERS gains python-apostrophe (a non-printed "it's" before
the print), printf (escaped `\n`) and echo (unquoted words), one-line
producers with no heredoc body: +1764 sink cases (20350 total).
main_verdicts.json regenerated with the CLI against the same baseline
da52aff8f4 (old allows unchanged, 1435 new allows).

Proof:
- new sink corpus cases alone: base 1435 violations of 1764, this tree 0
- test_lifecycle_guard_output_sink.py: base 11 failed (every new sink shape),
  this tree 77 passed
- heredoc_shape_corpus.py report --full: cases=20350 bash_ran=5192
  refused=17042 violations=0
- tests/cron: 2270 passed, 2 skipped; the 6 tests/tools + tests/hermes_cli
  files importing the guard or shell_heredoc: 502 passed
- scripts/check --base origin/main: ok
